# </custom_item>

# <custom_item>
#   type        : CONFIG_CHECK
#   description : "1.0048 - ASA - Ensure NTP authentication key is configured correctly"
#   info        : "Sets the key used to authenticate NTP servers Rationale: When authentication is not enabled, attackers can disguise as NTP servers and broadcast wrong time and it will be difficult to correlate events upon an incident."
#   solution    : "Step 1: Run the following to set the authentication key ID <key_id> hostname(config)# ntp trusted-key <key_id> Step 2: Run the following to configure the authentication key <authentication_key> hostname(config)# ntp authentication-key <key_id> md5 <authentication_key> Default Value: Disabled by default"
#   reference   : "NIST 800-53r5|AC-18 AU-7 AU-8 SC-23"
